1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:03,700
Football Intelligence Platform — Near-live, evidence-grounded match intelligence

2
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:08,360
This idea started when I studied the needs of an amateur football club.

3
00:00:08,360 --> 00:00:10,373
The club could record a match,

4
00:00:10,373 --> 00:00:14,733
but information that might influence football decisions was often unavailable during the game,

5
00:00:14,733 --> 00:00:15,740
delivered too late,

6
00:00:15,740 --> 00:00:18,759
or difficult to trust without checking the video again.

7
00:00:18,759 --> 00:00:28,150
I wanted to start at amateur level because clubs with the least money should still have access to the standard of evidence normally associated with top professional football.

8
00:00:28,150 --> 00:00:31,840
Coaches need more than footage. They need evidence they can use.

9
00:00:31,840 --> 00:00:34,638
The market broadly offers two approaches.

10
00:00:34,638 --> 00:00:39,769
Accessible camera platforms help clubs record, upload, stream and review matches,

11
00:00:39,769 --> 00:00:44,433
commonly through recurring cloud plans. Professional providers combine optical tracking,

12
00:00:44,433 --> 00:00:49,097
event data, analyst workflows and integrations, usually through bespoke contracts.

13
00:00:49,097 --> 00:00:51,429
Both approaches provide useful capabilities,

14
00:00:51,429 --> 00:00:56,560
but they serve very different budgets and levels of operational support.

15
00:00:56,560 --> 00:01:00,062
The downside is fragmentation. Capture, cloud storage, analysis,

16
00:01:00,062 --> 00:01:03,126
export and manual verification may remain separate.

17
00:01:03,126 --> 00:01:06,628
Costs increase as subscriptions and services are added,

18
00:01:06,628 --> 00:01:09,692
provider access and connectivity can become dependencies,

19
00:01:09,692 --> 00:01:14,507
and useful insight may arrive after the decision. Completed passes, possession,

20
00:01:14,507 --> 00:01:19,760
turnovers and shots matter most while the match can still be changed.

21
00:01:19,760 --> 00:01:23,627
Our alternative is one locally controlled and traceable flow.

22
00:01:23,627 --> 00:01:27,065
An elevated panoramic main camera preserves full-pitch geometry,

23
00:01:27,065 --> 00:01:29,214
team spacing and off-ball movement.

24
00:01:29,214 --> 00:01:32,222
Calibration connects image positions to the pitch.

25
00:01:32,222 --> 00:01:36,519
Local processing follows the ball and players, understands match state,

26
00:01:36,519 --> 00:01:39,527
calculates agreed events and delivers useful statistics.

27
00:01:39,527 --> 00:01:45,113
Every published number remains connected to its video evidence and exact rules-engine version.

28
00:01:45,113 --> 00:01:49,410
Additional cameras are added only when they create enough value.

29
00:01:49,410 --> 00:01:54,898
Today, the working proof processes prepared panoramic footage through calibration, tracking,

30
00:01:54,898 --> 00:01:59,887
football state, event review and regression-protected output. That is current.

31
00:01:59,887 --> 00:02:03,878
Live ingest, rolling match-day delivery, professional multi-camera operation,

32
00:02:03,878 --> 00:02:08,368
stadium deployment and durable player identity are next-stage capabilities.

33
00:02:08,368 --> 00:02:11,861
They are development targets, not completed claims.

34
00:02:11,861 --> 00:02:18,347
The controlled pilot target is at least ninety-five percent against independently reviewed references,

35
00:02:18,347 --> 00:02:21,340
reported separately for every agreed statistic.

36
00:02:21,340 --> 00:02:26,380
Operation starts with a rights-cleared panoramic feed and a camera calibration for that venue.

37
00:02:26,380 --> 00:02:30,700
The detector and tracker derive players and the ball from raw frames;

38
00:02:30,700 --> 00:02:33,940
no provider event file tells the engine what happened.

39
00:02:33,940 --> 00:02:37,540
The engine carries possession, match state and unresolved events forward.

40
00:02:37,540 --> 00:02:39,340
In the target live operation,

41
00:02:39,340 --> 00:02:45,820
a secured local GPU continuously ingests the feed and publishes each sixty-second update before the next is due.

42
00:02:45,820 --> 00:02:47,260
Duplicate events are suppressed,

43
00:02:47,260 --> 00:02:51,220
and the same evidence expands into a deeper half-time coaching view.

44
00:02:51,220 --> 00:02:54,577
Training and validation remain separate from match inference.

45
00:02:54,577 --> 00:02:58,772
Detection models are developed offline using appropriately licensed development data.

46
00:02:58,772 --> 00:03:02,548
Held-out annotations are revealed only after predictions are frozen;

47
00:03:02,548 --> 00:03:06,324
they never tell the engine what event to create.

48
00:03:06,324 --> 00:03:10,520
In the Review application, authorised validators inspect controlled video segments.

49
00:03:10,520 --> 00:03:13,037
Copilot contributes an independent video-based proposal,

50
00:03:13,037 --> 00:03:15,974
the rules engine contributes its own result,

51
00:03:15,974 --> 00:03:19,750
and provider annotations can provide a third post-inference check.

52
00:03:19,750 --> 00:03:23,527
A supported disagreement may improve only a general rule.

53
00:03:23,527 --> 00:03:29,820
Protected regressions then verify previous behaviour before the validated engine is deployed to new footage.

54
00:03:29,820 --> 00:03:34,284
The platform can be applied now to controlled post-match analysis,

55
00:03:34,284 --> 00:03:39,640
analyst-assisted segment review and an amateur or semi-professional pilot using prepared footage.

56
00:03:39,640 --> 00:03:44,550
The target installed core is below twelve thousand euros before tax:

57
00:03:44,550 --> 00:03:48,121
one panoramic camera, local GPU, storage, networking, installation,

58
00:03:48,121 --> 00:03:49,906
calibration and initial support.

59
00:03:49,906 --> 00:03:53,924
It requires neither cloud processing nor cloud video storage.

60
00:03:53,924 --> 00:03:55,263
Camera subscriptions recur,

61
00:03:55,263 --> 00:03:59,726
while bespoke professional packages can collectively reach thousands per month.

62
00:03:59,726 --> 00:04:04,190
The fair comparison is the complete three-year cost of ownership.

63
00:04:04,190 --> 00:04:07,972
Professional venues require synchronized camera feeds, sustained GPU throughput,

64
00:04:07,972 --> 00:04:10,914
resilient networking and storage, access control, monitoring,

65
00:04:10,914 --> 00:04:13,016
systems integration and match-day support.

66
00:04:13,016 --> 00:04:15,958
A second opposing panoramic view strengthens coverage;

67
00:04:15,958 --> 00:04:18,900
goal-end cameras can be added where justified.

68
00:04:18,900 --> 00:04:27,726
Future Query By Probability keeps the main camera continuous and consults only the relevant secondary view during a short low-confidence moment.

69
00:04:27,726 --> 00:04:31,508
Professional scale is therefore an engineering and operational programme,

70
00:04:31,508 --> 00:04:34,450
not simply the purchase of more cameras.

71
00:04:34,450 --> 00:04:39,699
We propose a staged co-development pilot between a professional football club and Xebia.

72
00:04:39,699 --> 00:04:44,141
Together we can define the statistics and targets, validate controlled matches,

73
00:04:44,141 --> 00:04:48,179
and build a route from grassroots affordability to professional performance.

74
00:04:48,179 --> 00:04:52,217
Xebia can help productionise edge processing, security, resilient live ingest,

75
00:04:52,217 --> 00:04:54,640
systems integration, monitoring and operational scale.

76
00:04:54,640 --> 00:04:59,082
The goal is not more data after the moment has passed.

77
00:04:59,082 --> 00:05:04,735
It is trusted football intelligence while the next decision can still change the match.

78
00:05:04,735 --> 00:05:08,773
Thank you for taking the time to review this vision.

79
00:05:08,773 --> 00:05:11,600
I hope we can build it together.

80
00:05:11,900 --> 00:05:17,300
Professional Football + Xebia — A staged co-development pilot

